path feature-step-link
kind flow
author ai
group features/cli
note step-link <name> <index> <target>: mark one step as the call site of the path named target, so a reader follows the link instead of reading the shared code's steps again in every path that reaches it. The agent needs it so shared code is mapped once in its own path and every path reaching it points there instead of copying its steps. index is the step index paths prints. An empty target is refused: step-unlink is the one way to remove a link. The target must exist and cannot be the step's own path; path --inline prints the linked path inline under the step.

